md='''# Batch84 independent local QA\n\nFixed commit: d7e1fed195c2c9fcb9690cdd52353b06b9edb261\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Glossopteris r001: PASS for five local stages.\n- Tide-dominated delta r002: REVISE (visual and specification).\n- Volcanic neck r003: PASS for five local stages.\n- Solution cave passage r005: maker BLOCKED, excluded from this review, not a fourth completed candidate.\n\nAll three: technical and pinned Three Node parsing pass. GPU and scene remain NOT RUN. No formal, user, website or release approval. Two local passes are not two releases.\n\n## Required delta correction\n\nThe channels really exist. Actual GLB coordinates, independent of material names, show a connected inlet-to-sea network and three downstream-widening mouths. At y=-3000m their low-channel widths are approximately994/1107/899m; at y=-3750m they widen to1113/1227/1007m.\n\nThe problem is visual construction: the76x80 regular grid leaves obvious131.58x150m bank teeth and coarse triangular tips. At512px the primary bar/channel pattern is much weaker in neutral material than in blue/tan color. Fresh neutral top corroborates this. Redistribute triangles from quiet flat terrain into channel-aligned continuous bank contours and controlled cross sections, preserving the original shallow scale, connectivity and widening. Do not fix it with color, depth bias, a favorable camera, arbitrary added relief or a new scientific scope. Keep this revision and its evidence intact, then perform targeted review on the actual repair.\n\n## Audit129: Glossopteris versus Bjuvia\n\nPersonally inspected the actual H.I.15 fossil photo, the actual Bjuvia simplex Fig11 photo (not its adjacent reconstruction), original concepts, both512px comparison frames and the candidate's eight final frames. Comparison-proof-2 uses exactly identical camera, framing, lights, material and scale. Decoded matrix and blade geometry are equal, generator bytes equal, vein geometry different. The test therefore does not win on outline, size, pose, color, damage, label or midrib.\n\nThe actual control has source-supported transverse near-parallel veins and basal forks. It is not blank: a fresh matched opposite-key diagnostic makes those veins plainly visible. Glossopteris retains oblique interconnected polygonal side relief. This supports the original qualitative topology distinction in the tested512px view.\n\nImportant limitation: the control is a normalized topology experiment, not a whole Bjuvia specimen or released asset. Its missing source outline is deliberately shared to eliminate silhouette as a cue.24 main rows per side heavily simplify both fields; control primary spacing5.98mm does not reproduce the source's12-14 veins/cm at physical scale. No measured density/relief or full-specimen fidelity is approved. This comparison cannot be repurposed as approval of a future Bjuvia model.\n\n## Neck and surfaces\n\nThe neck remains a steep, irregular roughly cylindrical solid over a lower eroded foot in all eight views. The top can look depressed because of shading, but actual crown center is highest at365m and the perimeter lies lower. No crater exists. Fresh source topology is closed, positive-volume and intersection-free. The nominal width is illustrative; the measured665.43m width is disclosed, not silently corrected to540m.\n\nDelta is likewise a closed single heightfield with zero nonadjacent intersections. Glossopteris is closed but intentionally overlaps blade/slab and embedded vein/junction volumes.10893 BVH contact pairs are recorded, not hidden or treated as an automatic failure. The full final views show no visible floating parts or z-fighting.\n\n## Verification and chronology\n\nAll633 manifested files match actual bytes and immutable Git blobs. Original inventory records, all premodel freeze entries, source references and configs are preserved. All24 final512px frames are personally inspected, hash-verified, and exactly match their lossless contact-sheet cells. Three fresh source reopen/re-exports are byte-identical. All project audits and default Khronos checks pass with zero errors/warnings; pinnedThree0.180.0 parses match counts/bounds. All six maker queue request/result/output chains independently revalidate with distinct PIDs, times, run IDs and fingerprints.\n\nFinal3 is a genuinely executed corrected render set after exact subject binding. Original incorrect/partial final sets and failed comparison history remain retained. Identical deterministic pixels alone do not imply copying. The original clock-domain note remains in force: provider generation timestamps and precise authoring-start time are unknown, not invented from mtimes. Schema policy classifier correction is not publication permission and did not change any active subject bytes.\n\nOwn evidence is compact, under30MB, and all heavy processes use the shared blocking lock with two Blender threads per process. No maker edits, clone/install, commit/push, PR/merge, website/CI, release or access/security changes. Detailed per-view observations, source URLs, hashes and seven separate stage states are in independent-qa.report.json.\n'''
(O/'REPORT.md').write_text(md)
